      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Switching a production inference endpoint (e.g., from TensorFlow Serving to Triton, or from a custom PyTorch script to TorchServe, or moving from CPU to GPU inference) is a high-stakes operation. The risks are not about \"missing deadlines\" but about silent data corruption, latency spikes, and resource exhaustion.\n\nHere is a risk register focused on **operational and model quality risks**.\n\n### Risk Register: Production Inference Runtime Migration\n\n| ID | Risk Description | Severity | Likelihood | Detection Method | Mitigation Strategy | Rollback Trigger |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **R1** | **Numerical Precision Drift**<br>New runtime uses different floating-point optimizations (e.g., TF32 on Ampere GPUs, or different batch norm folding) causing subtle output differences that don’t trigger errors but degrade model accuracy. | High | Medium | **Shadow Traffic Comparison:** Run 1% of production traffic through both old and new endpoints. Compare outputs using a tolerance threshold (e.g., max absolute difference > 1e-4). Monitor downstream business metrics (e.g., click-through rate) for anomalies. | 1. Disable aggressive optimizations (e.g., set `TF32=False` or disable FP16) during initial rollout.<br>2. Use deterministic algorithms where possible.<br>3. Validate against a golden dataset with known expected outputs. | If shadow traffic shows >0.1% of requests with output deviation > tolerance, OR if downstream business KPIs drop by >2% within 24 hours. |\n| **R2** | **Cold Start Latency Spikes**<br>New runtime has slower model loading or JIT compilation times, causing massive latency spikes during autoscaling events or initial traffic bursts. | High | High | **Latency Percentiles:** Monitor p99 and p99.9 latency during scale-up events. Alert if p99 exceeds SLA (e.g., 200ms) for >1 minute during scaling. | 1. Pre-warm instances by sending dummy requests before adding to load balancer.<br>2. Increase minimum replica count to reduce scaling frequency.<br>3. Use model caching (e.g., persistent volume claims) to speed up load times. | If p99 latency exceeds SLA by >50% for >5 minutes during a scaling event, OR if"
      },
      "finish_reason": "length"
    }
  ],
